@ybbmm/dsh-translation-pane README · Provider failover and health：The two anonymous endpoints are independent services, and a network that can
reach one may be unable to reach the other. The direct route therefore treats a
provider-level failure as a routing problem rather than a dead end:

@ybbmm/dsh-translation-pane README · Resilience：Fragments of one long document are dispatched with bounded concurrency rather
than one at a time, so a large input is not many times slower than it needs to
be.

@ybbmm/dsh-translation-pane README · Error codes：The Host raises `provider-unreachable` when its own network cannot reach the
provider, while `offline` is the browser losing its Host. Keeping them apart
matters: only the second one is fixed by checking that the Host is running.
